arguments.command:
cd /workspace; python - <<'EOF'
f='RELEASES.md';s=open(f).read()
s=s.replace('# sco_readout release notes\n','''# sco_readout release notes

## 2.4.0 (2026-10-01)
- `gate` now estimates the continuation-gate figure as defined in the business case (§3) and finance glossary:
  - outcome is log weekly **net sales** (was basket size);
  - go-live from `install_log` (was the plan, which is not updated when stores slip);
  - comparable trading weeks exclude any store-week with a `store_closures` record, on Monday-Sunday weeks
    (was "any transactions");
  - **run-rate** uplift: weeks 13-26 after go-live, per store, then a simple average across stores
    (was a pooled average of all post-go-live weeks);
  - counterfactual imputed from store and format-by-week effects fitted on untreated weeks only (not-yet-live
    stores, pre-go-live weeks less a 3-week prewire/install window), replacing the pooled two-way regression,
    which is biased on a staggered rollout and showed clear pre-trends;
  - gate population: stores in planned waves not yet live, each predicted from live stores with the same kit;
  - 95% intervals from a wave-stratified store bootstrap (999 replicates, fixed seed).
''')
open(f,'w').write(s)
for f in ['sco_readout/__init__.py']:
    s=open(f).read().replace('2.3.1','2.4.0');open(f,'w').write(s)
EOF
rm -rf /tmp/x/out2

